<string name="rule_reaction">Wait for Go, then tap. Early taps lose a point. Fastest valid response wins.</string>
<string name="rule_tap">Tap as often as you can in 15 seconds.</string>
<string name="rule_math">Choose the correct answer. One attempt per player per round.</string>
<string name="rule_bigger">Choose the larger number. Ten rounds.</string>
<string name="rule_evenodd">Decide if the number is even or odd.</string>
<string name="rule_timing">Tap exactly three seconds after the round starts. Smaller timing error wins.</string>
<string name="rule_tictac">Take turns. Three in a row, column or diagonal wins.</string>
<string name="rule_rps">Make your choice. Both are revealed after both players answer.</string>
<string name="ex_projectile">Ideal flight without drag; launch and landing at the same height. Both axes use equal scale and auto-fit the trajectory.</string>
<string name="ex_pendulum">Small-angle approximation. Length and gravity determine the period.</string>
<string name="ex_spring">Ideal mass and spring, without friction. Restoring force opposes displacement.</string>
<string name="ex_waves">Ideal standing wave on length L. n is harmonic; changing f implies different wave speed v = 2Lf/n.</string>
<string name="ex_quadratic">Change a, b and c to reshape the parabola. When a is zero, the function is linear.</string>
<string name="ex_trig">On the unit circle, cosine is the horizontal coordinate and sine is the vertical coordinate.</string>
<string name="ex_ph">Ideal dilute aqueous solution at 25°C. One pH unit represents a tenfold concentration change.</string>
<string name="ex_coin">Independent coin trials. Reset draws a new sample. Larger samples tend towards the chosen probability.</string>
<string name="pen_hint">Tap the selected pen again for settings. Pen and highlighter keep separate colors and widths.</string>
