<string name="ex_ohm">Ideal DC resistor: I = V/R; power P = VI. Schematic drawing.</string>
<string name="ex_energy">Classical translational energy: E = ½mv². Doubling speed quadruples energy. Arrow indicates speed.</string>
<string name="ex_buoyancy">Fully submerged displaced volume in uniform fluid. F = ρgV; g = 9.81 m/s². Floating equilibrium is not modeled.</string>
<string name="ex_lens">Thin converging lens, paraxial approximation. Positive v: real/inverted; negative v: virtual/upright. At u=f the image is at infinity. Auto-scaled drawing clips tall images.</string>
<string name="ex_triangle_area">A = bh/2. The vertical colored segment marks perpendicular height.</string>
<string name="ex_statistics">Three equally weighted values. μ is mean; σ is population SD (divide by 3), not sample SD.</string>
<string name="ex_gas">Ideal gas at equilibrium: PV = nRT. Temperature: kelvin; volume: liters; pressure: kPa. Particles are schematic.</string>
<string name="ex_dilution">Nonreacting solute, additive volumes: C₂ = C₁V₁/(V₁ + water). Educational model, not a real chemical preparation guide.</string>
